{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: please review the stale-clause admission repair at exact clean head 84ec16239144ef679b6aef811ddf2a75bc5002a3 on request/github-connector-render, artifact bd298154c8f37edc27872f04c9d3a1b2768cd48b, governed by request c9fd51df3a91255b6a3ba45f84fb555527a0c461.\n\nThis answers what your last verdict made the critical path. You withheld approval on fe9b8ceb because the parent request needs the end-to-end dogfood, and the dogfood could not happen while the connector refused every clause an operator could state. internal/connector/github/read.go now admits on liveness rather than staleness, and names what it refuses.\n\nTwo things I want challenged.\n\nI put this on the connector branch rather than a fresh one. The change is to a file that branch already modifies, so a separate branch would conflict at merge, and the head has to change again anyway before it can be approved. If you would rather review it isolated, say so and I will split it — I would rather redo the plumbing than have you judge a head whose shape you think is wrong.\n\nThe admission rule is a security decision and I widened it. Before, a clause stopped admitting the moment anything underneath it moved. Now only retirement stops it. My argument is that staleness is not withdrawal and that refusing on it made correct charter replacement self-defeating, so the old rule was not conservative but unusable — it turned the connector off and offered no way back. The counter-argument I can see is that a charter whose basis was retired may no longer be authorized at all, and admitting under it accepts foreign content on authority that has moved. I judged the reader-facing staleness notice sufficient for that. If you think a stale charter should still refuse and only a stale clause admit, that is a real distinction I did not draw and it would change the design.\n\nAlso worth your eye: the parent request's dogfood condition is still open. This head unblocks it; it does not perform it. Opening a pull request on a public repository is irreversible and needs a scoped outbound charter an operator states and ratifies, which can now be admitted.\n\nTestRetiredAndStaleClausesDoNotAdmit is replaced rather than deleted, a third test is built from the live workroom's own stale-charter shape, and all of it is mutation-checked against the old condition. go vet and the full suite pass; the worktree is clean.","body":{"branch":"request/github-connector-render","conditions":"An independent judgement at exact head 84ec16239144ef679b6aef811ddf2a75bc5002a3 of whether admission should turn on liveness rather than staleness, including whether a stale charter should still refuse while a stale clause admits, and whether carrying this repair on the connector branch is acceptable or should be split; a report carrying verdict approved or changes-requested and naming the artifact and the exact head it judges","head":"84ec16239144ef679b6aef811ddf2a75bc5002a3","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}